          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fc60796f86d3bdc9808d0de8d4bdf3790224b9405cdffbe7dc0fe906c461d311:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_83951cb95ec04f62a67cecc7700a7552",
      "statement": "Retired config.toml sections ([slack], [telegram]) parse without error, emitting deprecation notices. Presence of setup keys (signing_secret_env, bot_token_env, installation_id, etc.) fails boot closed with migration guidance. The entrypoint auto-migrates the old-shipped [slack] enabled=false stub.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/app/ironclaw_config/src/retired_sections.rs#L1-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:52d05703af14c86b5eee500973c5e86d7317629a8b8b09e69bfe85cbb35a802a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docker/reborn/entrypoint.sh#L246-L289",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:860a8ffbea914a9bfcfb5904e3424961ac70a8133ad536002d095225aff9eb8b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_590e324fe2ca4608be33f1dbc4267ca2",
      "statement": "On first boot, if config.toml is missing, the entrypoint selects a default config by profile (from /opt/ironclaw/reborn/config*.toml), copies it into $IRONCLAW_REBORN_HOME/config.toml, and preserves it on subsequent boots. Custom configs can be mounted at /opt/ironclaw/ and selected via IRONCLAW_REBORN_DEFAULT_CONFIG.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docker/reborn/entrypoint.sh#L134-L180",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:28c16fb52f8eb8eb3ffe1a26dfd4a7a74d62f49b05e51eb3bba2e80fb8335449:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_313e91493d9248c89ef6b96a53450da7",
      "statement": "The PostgreSQL backend uses a connection pool sized by IRONCLAW_REBORN_POSTGRES_POOL_MAX_SIZE. For managed Postgres providers with low session-pool caps, setting this to 1 or 2 prevents exhaustion. Migration connection timeout is controlled by IRONCLAW_FILESYSTEM_POSTGRES_MIGRATION_CONNECT_MAX_WAIT_SECS (default 5 minutes).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/internal/reborn/deploy-reborn-cli-docker.md#L138-L148",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5f4d4fed498da403f9be7d368f7076b48c79936aa4f6e6bcadb4069f2ff09b41:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9141f4553dc841fb8b4fbcbebc1389dd",
      "statement": "Railway deployments set IRONCLAW_REBORN_SERVE_HOST=0.0.0.0 (Railway NAT), IRONCLAW_REBORN_PROFILE to hosted-single-tenant or hosted-single-tenant-volume, and either IRONCLAW_REBORN_POSTGRES_URL or a mounted volume. The container exposes /api/health for Railway healthchecks; the WebUI listener starts before database assembly completes, allowing graceful drains.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/internal/reborn/deploy-reborn-cli-docker.md#L75-L126",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8069a100eb0ec99302de8253e585afb46236d4f12182f64bce1a5396c033d745:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_df7b6f97761e471da0c714ecb49f6263",
      "statement": "The ironclaw CLI binary is a single monolithic package that includes all concrete extension packages (Slack, Telegram, web-app), first-party capabilities (Google, memory-native), WebUI, and composition runtime. There are no separate service binaries; the binary is the sole entrypoint. Dependencies are pinned in crates/app/ironclaw_cli/Cargo.toml and validated by architecture tests.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/app/ironclaw_cli/Cargo.toml#L26-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b21c66744587fc048558b45a5e98f45b8f48c0de0faf01a511350d4a9fd11423:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/app/ironclaw_cli/README.md#L1-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6aa0c58508a6e3560e48558acb42744be3af9c7557a436251746bd9e7d6e030d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e16ae22fb780463ca5003f5831b7c0f6",
      "statement": "The composition root (crates/app/ironclaw_composition) is the sole assembly entry point. build_reborn_runtime() assembles the full runtime stack based on deployment profile, storage backend, and host bindings. Composition is service-shaped (never owns domain logic) and checked for readiness fail-closed on production/migration-dry-run profiles.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/app/ironclaw_composition/README.md#L1-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c0569233b0906bd6d7c7b7c77711a2d6560b8ca0bca18bfaf0efce089c67567f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/app/ironclaw_composition/src/lib.rs#L1-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:104adf7bf30ad36846e43e989de94f3153f0e14799622c0524eab46f0ed0511f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_02a855bfc3a042e7b5eae15258eb79f2",
      "statement": "The DeploymentConfig struct controls sandbox type (None/Docker/Railway Sandbox), storage backend (libSQL/PostgreSQL), policy profile (Standalone/HostedSingleTenant/Production), and traffic policy (Enabled/Disabled/HealthcheckOnly). These are policy data, not behavior; the runtime policy resolver (ironclaw_runtime_policy) is the only producer of EffectiveRuntimePolicy.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/app/ironclaw_composition/src/deployment.rs#L1-L100",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:15b98912a2f6a1951edce1fcec162b6b53d67b5117dc5d716571b69b3883013c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cc3c7b4ce68c40aab37abc3236ee54e6",
      "statement": "Slack webhooks are compiled unconditionally into the image and answer 503 temporarily_unavailable until the extension's signing secret is registered in WebUI /extensions. There is no IRONCLAW_REBORN_SLACK_ENABLED variable (no reader exists) and no [slack] section should be added to config.toml. Legacy [slack] sections must be deleted or the entrypoint must migrate them.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/internal/reborn/deploy-reborn-cli-docker.md#L245-L295",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:303d9b1a64171ac00bd98c30420361800f13946475064543a4a634092b928163:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7e958a6e28134ae99414c6bab57802a2",
      "statement": "The ironclaw binary is compiled with optional features: memory-mem0 (third-party mem0 provider), test-support (loopback OAuth for hermetic tests). Without memory-mem0, mem0 bindings fail closed. Release builds fail closed if test-support seam environment variables are present.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/app/ironclaw_cli/Cargo.toml#L26-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1e6dae849d54ff6260784a82548c4d2510f03dd67d84bb677b6812117da2221a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_66f0694bfdd54599bf8876f3a494db72",
      "statement": "ironclaw serve command starts by assembling the deployment, instantiating the product surface (runtime, LLM gateway, turn coordinator), binding the WebUI listener, and spawning turn-runner workers. On hosted-single-tenant profiles, the HTTP listener starts before database assembly completes, returning 503 for non-health routes until the router is ready.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/app/ironclaw_cli/README.md#L25-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5cf3da42236d25eb86317dffdd61dd155f0ac236448e83b4a1037c73c95d0c1:"
        },
        {
